                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.05/214: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Perkins</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-12-21T11:00:00+08:00">December 21, 1929—11
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received December 21—6:45 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>1178. My 1165, December 18, 5 p.m. Following from Jacobs and Bucknell: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“December 20, 10 a.m. Referring to the alternative proposal of the
                            Chinese delegation for consular representation on the court, telegraphed
                            by the British Consulate General at Shanghai yesterday to the interested
                            Senior Minister, the chief of the Chinese delegation stated today that
                            it was an official alternative proposal. We submit that this also does
                            not provide the necessary safeguards.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Perkins</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
